※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4533

※ A reference names somewhere, so what follows `&` has to be something that is
※ somewhere: a name, a variable at the top level, an element of an array.  A
※ value the program worked out is in no particular place -- it may be in a
※ register and it may be nowhere at all -- so there is nothing to name.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = 1u8
    let r: &u8 = &(n + 2u8)
    let m: u8 = r⌖
    0u6
